\title{phylloptim: leaf gas exchange with explicit plant hydraulics}
\description{
A leaf gas-exchange model in which stomatal behaviour emerges from
hydraulics. Farquhar-von Caemmerer-Berry photosynthesis is coupled to an
explicit soil-root-stem-leaf water path, and the operating point is the
maximum of an optimality objective over the root-collar water potential.
Nine optimality models share one solver; \code{\link[=cost_curve_names]{cost_curve_names()}} lists them.
The model is a set of R-free C++ headers under \code{inst/include}, and this
package is an R layer on top of them.
}
\section{Where to start}{

\itemize{
\item Solve a leaf in one call: \code{\link[=leaf_solve]{leaf_solve()}}, with \code{\link[=leaf_traits]{leaf_traits()}} and
\code{\link[=leaf_control]{leaf_control()}}.
\item Keep a leaf and drive it yourself: \code{\link[=leaf_model]{leaf_model()}}, \code{\link[=set_drivers]{set_drivers()}},
\code{\link[=set_traits]{set_traits()}} and \code{\link[=operating_point]{operating_point()}}.
\item Trait gradients: \code{\link[=leaf_gradient]{leaf_gradient()}} for one operating point, and
\code{\link[=leaf_batch]{leaf_batch()}} with \code{\link[=leaf_gradient_batch]{leaf_gradient_batch()}} for a fit over many
observations.
\item Thermal damage: \code{\link[=leaf_damage_trajectory]{leaf_damage_trajectory()}} and \code{\link[=leaf_damage_gradient]{leaf_damage_gradient()}}.
\item Vulnerability curves from published quantities: \code{\link[=weibull_p50_c]{weibull_p50_c()}} and
\code{\link[=psi_at_plc]{psi_at_plc()}}.
}
